From 3d4814a91b897e636ad8f82c25bfa611509ff3bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 17:23:33 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 06/14] configstore: tenant-scope Name uniqueness on providers,
 keys, MCP clients
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Closes the Phase 1 schema rollout. Two tenants can now independently
register a provider named "openai", an MCP client named "tools", a key
named "production", etc — without colliding.

Index restructure:
  - drop legacy single-column unique indexes:
      idx_config_providers_name
      idx_config_mcp_clients_name
      idx_key_name
  - replace with composite (tenant_id, name) unique indexes:
      idx_providers_tenant_name
      idx_mcp_tenant_name
      idx_key_tenant_name

Caller update (must ship in the same patch):
  RDBConfigStore.UpdateProvidersConfig upsert now lists
  (tenant_id, name) as its OnConflict target. Dropping the old
  single-column index without this change broke TestFullVirtualKeyFlow
  with "ON CONFLICT clause does not match any PRIMARY KEY or UNIQUE
  constraint" in the patch 0009 draft — splitting the index change
  from the caller change was not viable.

Out of scope (stays globally unique):
  - config_mcp_clients.client_id — FK target for TableOauthUserToken;
    a composite FK would cascade through the oauth tables.
  - config_keys.key_id — UUID, doesn't benefit from per-tenant scoping.

NOT in this patch: the broader query layer refactor (Get/Update/Delete
methods accepting a tenant_id argument). Until those land, the
GetProvider*ByName / GetMCPClientByName paths still take the first
matching row across all tenants — runtime isolation in the per-tenant
Bifrost dispatch layer is what keeps reads scoped today.

Test: TestMigrationTenantScopedNameUniques_PerTenantUniqueness
asserts the legacy indexes are gone, the composites are present, two
tenants can register the same Name on each table, intra-tenant
uniqueness still holds, and ClientID stays globally unique.

Full framework/configstore + plugins/governance + multitenant test
suites pass.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
